<!--
  <sui-accordion> — SUI port of <ship-accordion>.
  Declarative accordion with single or multiple open mode.

  Prop parity vs <ship-accordion>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                          SUI                      Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  type ('single'|'multiple',   type (string, 'single',  ✓ feat/next declares
    'single')                    reflect)                 this as a free string
                                                          (not a closed enum) —
                                                          kept exactly as-is,
                                                          not tightened, so an
                                                          off-list value keeps
                                                          falling through to
                                                          "multiple" behavior
                                                          in the controller,
                                                          same as today.
  value (string, '')           value (string, '',       ✓ comma-sep open vals
                                 reflect)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ship-change → {value}        sui-change → {value}     event renamed
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  slots: (default) items       (default) items          ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from the feat/next baseline, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No tone/size channel here — nothing to delete/globalize.
  - No L1 controls — this is a plain slotted container.
  - `type`/`value` are both free strings with `reflect`; the new
    component-object prop shorthand can't express reflect on a plain
    string (it only auto-reflects tone/size/unions/bools — see
    sui-alert's dismissible/tone for the shapes it DOES cover), so both
    stay declared via the plain prop directive, unchanged from
    feat/next.
  - The host's own surface (bordered rounded panel) moves to a host-sx
    directive — the closed-vocabulary equivalent of the old bare
    `:host{border;radius;overflow;background}` block. `display:block`
    and `[hidden]` are dropped: framework-owned now (BASE_CSS).
  - `::slotted(sui-accordion-item:not(:first-child))` stays in <style> —
    sx/variants have no reach into slotted descendants.
-->

<prop name="type" type="string" default="single" reflect />
<prop name="value" type="string" default="" reflect />

<host sx="border:border radius:lg overflow:hidden bg:surface-1" />

<style>
  ::slotted(sui-accordion-item:not(:first-child)) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
</style>

<slot></slot>
